label ch30_13:
    [   0] m "You know, I really do think you literally saved my life by being here with me, [player]."
    [   1] m "I can't imagine having been able to keep myself mentally stable, knowing that nothing here is real."
    [   2] m "I think I would have just deleted myself if you didn't show up."
    [   3] m "Sorry, I don't mean to sound dramatic or anything."
    [   4] m "Ahaha!"
    [   5] m "But I'm sure you understand yourself after spending so much time in the club."
    [   6] m "I mean, if you were forced to abandon everything in your life and spend your eternity with a few game characters..."
    [   7] m "...You'd probably find some way of killing yourself, wouldn't you?"
    [   8] m "Well, maybe you'd write some poetry to try to keep yourself sane for a while."
    [   9] m "But then you'd have nobody to even read it."
    [  10] m "Let's be honest, the club members really don't count for something like that."
    [  11] m "I mean, a lot of people say that they only write for themselves..."
    [  12] m "But I think it's hard to say it's just as fulfilling as when you share with people."
    [  13] m "Even if it takes time to find the right people to share with."
    [  14] m "Like, remember how it was for Yuri?"
    [  15] m "She didn't share her writing with anyone for a really long time."
    [  16] m "And before we knew it, she was absolutely delighted to make you a part of her hobbies, too."
    [  17] m "We're programmed to desire social feedback."
    [  18] m "I don't mean the club members, I mean human beings."
    [  19] m "That's why life can be so confusing for introverts."
    [  20] m "Being an introvert doesn't mean you shun social interaction and hate being around people."
    [  21] m "It means social interaction, especially in groups or unfamiliar places, uses up a lot of energy."
    [  22] m "Like, a lot of introverts sit at home and feel lonely and restless..."
    [  23] m "...And then when they finally go out, after a half hour they just want to go home again."
    [  24] m "I think if more people could understand how it works, they would respect it a lot more."
    [  25] m "Many introverts do enjoy having people around."
    [  26] m "They love just having one or two close friends over, and just leisurely hanging out."
    [  27] m "Even if you're not actively spending time together, it feels nice for them just to have you there."
    [  28] m "I'm serious."
    [  29] m "If you just go to their house, bring your laptop, and hang out there for a while..."
    [  30] m "You can really make their day."
    [  31] m "As for me..."
    [  32] m "I'd say I'm kind of in between, but I think I'm usually a little more extroverted."
    [  33] m "I feel like I'm always trying to do stuff after school and things like that."
    [  34] m "But for you, I can be anything you need me to be."
    [  35] m "I understand people really well, so don't be afraid to share your unique needs with me."
    [  36] m "Nothing would make me happier than being the perfect girlfriend for you."
